  "term": "amyloid precursor protein",
  "definition": "Amyloid precursor protein is a human protein made from the APP gene that helps with signaling at the cell surface. It is cut by secretases into several different products, including soluble peptides, membrane-bound pieces, amyloid plaque components, transcription-related molecules, and fragments that can be toxic to nerve cells.",
